[{"order":1,"type":"heading","text":"Tutorial: Mocking Final Classes and Methods in Mockito"},{"order":2,"type":"paragraph","text":"By default, Mockito cannot mock final classes or final methods due to the limitations of Java's dynamic proxy generation. However, starting from version 2.10.0, Mockito introduced an opt-in incubation feature that leverages the Byte Buddy library to enable this capability. This tutorial covers how to configure and use Mockito to mock final components."},{"order":3,"type":"subheading","text":"Prerequisites and Configuration"},{"order":4,"type":"paragraph","text":"To enable mocking of final classes and methods, you must configure Mockito's inline mocking feature. This is done by creating a configuration file in your test resources directory."},{"order":5,"type":"bullet_point","text":"Create a file named 'mockito-extensions/org.mockito.plugins.MockMaker' under your 'src/test/resources' directory."},{"order":6,"type":"bullet_point","text":"Add the following single line of text inside that file: 'mock-maker-inline'."},{"order":7,"type":"code","text":"# Content of src/test/resources/mockito-extensions/org.mockito.plugins.MockMaker
mock-maker-inline"},{"order":8,"type":"subheading","text":"Example Scenario: Final Class and Method"},{"order":9,"type":"paragraph","text":"Consider the following final class with a final method that we want to test and mock:"},{"order":10,"type":"code","text":"public final class PaymentService {
    public final boolean processPayment(double amount) {
        // Complex payment gateway logic
        return false;
    }
}"},{"order":11,"type":"subheading","text":"Writing the Test with Mockito"},{"order":12,"type":"paragraph","text":"With the 'mock-maker-inline' extension enabled, you can write standard Mockito tests for final classes and final methods without throwing any exceptions."},{"order":13,"type":"code","text":"import org.junit.jupiter.api.Test;
import org.mockito.Mockito;
import static org.junit.jupiter.api.Assertions.assertTrue;

public class PaymentServiceTest {

    @Test
    public void testMockFinalClass() {
        // Create a mock of the final class
        PaymentService paymentServiceMock = Mockito.mock(PaymentService.class);

        // Stub the final method
        Mockito.when(paymentServiceMock.processPayment(100.0)).thenReturn(true);

        // Verify behavior
        assertTrue(paymentServiceMock.processPayment(100.0));
    }
}"},{"order":14,"type":"subheading","text":"Conclusion"},{"order":15,"type":"paragraph","text":"By activating the inline mock maker via the MockMaker configuration file, Mockito gains the ability to subclass final classes and override final methods at runtime. This removes traditional design constraints in legacy codebases and makes unit testing much more flexible."}]
